// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_SECRET_EXFILTRATION
// Completion Blueprint Phase 4 (2026-08-15), CodeRabbit review guard: a bare EGRESS BUILTIN
// (`send`) stored into a struct field by place-assignment, read back, and applied to a secret
// argument. The danger is that `g` IS the egress, not that it returns a labeled value — so it is
// NOT handled by the `fn_alias`/`field_fn_identities` identity lane (builtins carry no user
// identity name). It is caught by the independent `field_builtin_gate_tags` lane, which records
// the EgressSink tag of a field-stored builtin and is consulted by the sink check. This fixture
// locks that coverage so the two lanes cannot drift: the identity-lane fix for row 6 must not be
// mistaken for the sink-builtin-carrier mechanism, which lives in the gate-tags lane.
struct Box { f: u64 }
fn key() -> secret<i64> { return 42; }
fn main() uses(net.send) {
    let b = Box { f: 0 };
    b.f = send;
    let g = b.f;
    g("host", 80, key());
}
